}

Even with no errors the bound reaches \code{alpha} only from
\code{n_min = ceiling(log(delta) / log(1 - alpha))} items: 59 at \code{alpha = 0.05}
and 299 at \code{alpha = 0.01}, with \code{delta = 0.05}. For
\code{"error_among_accepted"} the sequence therefore starts at the strictest
threshold that acts on at least \code{n_min} items; that count uses only the
scores, not the labels, so starting there keeps the guarantee. For
\code{"miss_rate"} the set needs at least \code{n_min} items on which acting is
wrong.

